-- title:
--   Kernel polynomial of ⟨ P⟩ divides ψ_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and $\ell$ a prime natural number with $\ell \neq 2$, so that $\ell$ is odd. Assume that $\ell \cdot \Delta(W)$ is a unit in $T$, where $\Delta(W)$ is the discriminant of $W$, and let $x \in T$ be a root of the $\ell$-th pre-division polynomial, i.e. $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x) = 0$. Then there is a family $r \colon \mathbb{N} \to T$ with the following three properties. First, for every $a$ with $1 \le a \le (\ell-1)/2$ the value $(\Psi^2_a)(x)$ is a unit of $T$ and $r_a \cdot (\Psi^2_a)(x) = (\Phi_a)(x)$; since $\Psi^2_a$ and $\Phi_a$ are the univariate division-polynomial data computing the abscissa of a multiple, $r_a$ is the $x$-coordinate of $[a]P$ for a point $P$ with abscissa $x$, and it is uniquely determined by the displayed equation. Second, for all $a, b$ with $1 \le a, b \le (\ell-1)/2$ and $a \neq b$, the difference $r_a - r_b$ is a unit of $T$. Third, the monic polynomial $\prod_{a=1}^{(\ell-1)/2} (X - r_a)$ divides $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ in $T[X]$. Here $(\ell-1)/2$ is truncated natural division, and the product is indexed by the interval $\mathrm{Icc}\,1\,((\ell-1)/2)$.
--
--   The polynomial $\prod_{a}(X - r_a)$ is the kernel polynomial of the cyclic subgroup generated by a point of exact order $\ell$ with abscissa $x$, in the sense of Vélu and Kohel, formulated over an arbitrary base ring in which $\ell\Delta(W)$ is invertible. It is used to pass from a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-structure to the associated cyclic subgroup of order $\ell$, and is cited in the construction of [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Link.of_map_of_surjective_of_ker_pow_eq_bot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IsGamma1Link.of_map_of_surjective_of_ker_pow_eq_bot).
